A||N||12||1slow60||ECM wont go closed loop     help||||1||
Z||000000||1slow60||12-25-2001||01:00 AM||||  Alright guys i am new here as far as posting but I have been lurking for a while and reading what ya'll know about the old 2.8s and computers.  I problem is in a 86 firebird, iknow its not a fiero but the same computer system so i hope that someone can help me.  I swapped in a 88 350 from a computer and wiring harness from the donor vehicle.  Now the motor wont go closed loop.  It has a hypertech chip in it that was there wheni bought the donor vehicle.  I replaced the plugs, wires, oxygen sensor, and the temp sender from the cylander head.  At the moment The motor will get up to operating temp of 210 - 230 degrees with the O2 sensor running at round 440mv and up too 211 o2 crosscounts and never go into closed loop.  I checked the wiring several times and believe that it is right including the grounds.  I have had a multitude of codes but right now it seems to be be code 13 oxygen sensor and code 44 lean exhaust.  I followed the christmas trees in the swap book that i have and ran into a snag there with the o2 circuit.  The test under code 13 says to ground the O2 sensor wire and start the vehicle with the ALDL A and B terminals grounded and watch the check engine light to see if it stops flashing within 4 seconds.  I past this test but checked the sensor voltage anyways.  It was at .3 volts.  Right on the money.  The book says the the computer is good.  Now go to code 44 and it says to perform the same test but now it says that if the check engine light goes out that the computer is bad.  Both are GM flow charts so which is correct.  I hate the thought of buying another computer for nothing.  What else tells the computer to go closed loop asides from the 105 degrees in the coolant system and the O2 sensor warming up to operating temp?  One last thing that might be part of this puzzle is the fact that i am running a 5 speed with an auto PROM.  I installed the VSS and all that and it is working fine but do i need to do anything with the tc lock up wiring that originally ran to the transmission?  Again I know its not a fiero but i appreciate any help that ya'll can give me on this.  I am about out of ideas on it.  thanks.||||reg||1
