Z||000010||Bazooka||12-25-2001||10:40 AM||||Slow60,    Everything seems to be pointing to the Prom unit or the ECM. Normally you can have a code of 51, 52, 53 or 54 for the bad ECM or prom. The parameters that you are using for closed loop activation are OK and the O2, CTS, and the 2-3 minute running time are the only ones that I have heard in these early GM's. If you haven't done so already, I would first "Backprobe" the computer for the correct values to eliminate wiring/connector problems at the CTS and O2 sensors and the computer inputs. If those readings look normal, head over to the junkyard and get a used ECM with a regular prom chip for $25. You can interchange the performance chip later. Also match the used unit with the manual trans, etc that you now have. By the way, is this a Feedback carburetor or TPI system?<BR>    I'd be looking for anything that would prevent the electrical signal from being sent back to the ECM. The next time you warm up the engine, you might see if you can invoke a rich signal at the O2 sensor by pulling off the PCV valve temporarily and note the change in the O2 volts. Or by inducing a lean signal by pulling off one of the wires from the spark plugs momentarily and again check the change in O2 volts. That would confirm that there is a response from the engine operation and the O2 sensor. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||terryk||12-25-2001||11:46 AM||||Rev the engine at 3000 RPM for 3 minutes and check for closed loop. Sounds like the O2 isn't hot enough.<P>If it does and assuming the O2 is good, but may have to switch to a heated O2.<P>Merry Christmas!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||1slow60||12-25-2001||01:27 PM||||  Thanks guys.  Right now i get a rich reading at idle through the scanner at a constant RPM when the motor is idling.  The second that you touch the gas the scanner says that it is lean.  My oxygen sensor mv never get to 500 mv so I am alittle confused about that one.  For a new test today that i havent tried i unhooked the vacuum line to the fuel preasure regulator that if my reading is right should raise the fuel preasure.  More fuel preasure equels richer mix right?  I have had the mot hot enough to start perculating the water in the radiator so I dont beleave that the motor isnt getting hot enough for the O2 sensor to activate.  Especially with 211 crosscounts.  The factory o2 sensor is mounted in the exhaust manifold where the four cylanders become one.  Guess that you could call it the collector on the stock manifold.  Probably no more than 4"s from the exhaust port.  Where can I find a listing of exact values for ECM connectors at?  I have been chasing wires throughout the engine harness and I think that they are fine but I would love to check the ECM values.  I would get a used computer for the car but I havent seen a TPI in the boneyard since I have been in Cali and the 350 didnt come with a 5 speed.  That means either a 305 PROM with a 5 speed or a 350 auto prom.  Does anyone know if a TBI prom will fire the injectors on a TPI?  After all all 4 injectors on one bank fire at the same time.  Atleast on some models.  But thanks again for the responses.<p>[This message has been edited by 1slow60 (edited 12-25-2001).]||||reg||1
